                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe0d7791-cf02-4b2c-810d-2529e308a3d2",
                                                "sense_id": "028bd18c-7777-3803-99a4-ee073b72865b",
                                                "text": "So, it seems clear that the idiosyncratic restrictions relating to the range of\n complements which a Preposition does or does not permit are directly analo-\n gous to the parallel restrictions which hold in the case of Verbs. The restric-\ntions concerned are not categorial in nature (i.e. they are not associated with\n every single item belonging to a given category): on the contrary, they are\n lexical in nature (that is to say, they are properties of individual lexical items,\n so that different words belonging to the same category permit a different range\n of complements)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d0287542-7974-3f9d-8212-cd35ec1adea7",
                                        "entry_id": "ab670b0d-691e-3ffb-bce3-74c51c30f441",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Concerning lexicography or a lexicon or dictionary."
